        "title": "Botany - Overview: The Plant Kingdom",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Plants are the primary energy transducers of life on Earth — converting solar photons into chemical energy that all heterotrophs depend on. They colonized land ~470 million years ago and transformed the planet: building soil, oxygenating the atmosphere, creating forests that drove carbon burial and climate stabilization."
    },
