        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Botany - Overview: The Plant Kingdom",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nPLANT KINGDOM PHYLOGENY AND KEY INNOVATIONS\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#004",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:botany:00-overview, git-history:botany:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "botany/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "botany/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:botany:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "botany",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "botany",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Botany - Overview: The Plant Kingdom",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "CHAROPHYTE ALGAE (green algae, aquatic)\n    │   Shared features: chlorophyll a+b, starch storage, cell plate division\n    │   Land colonization: ~470 Mya (Ordovician)\n    ▼\nBRYOPHYTES — no vascular tissue\n├── Mosses (Bryophyta)\n├── Liverworts (Marchantiophyta)     ← Innovation: CUTICLE (water retention)\n└── Hornworts (Anthocerotophyta)     ← Innovation: STOMATA (gas exchange)\n    │\n    ▼\nVASCULAR PLANTS (Tracheophyta) — xylem + phloem\n├── Lycophytes (clubmosses, quillworts)\n├── Monilophytes (ferns, horsetails)  ← Innovation: VASCULAR TISSUE (height)\n│       Carboniferous coal swamps: 30m tree ferns\n│\n└── SEED PLANTS (Spermatophyta)\n    │   ← Innovation: SEEDS (embryo protection, desiccation tolerance)\n    │   ← Innovation: POLLEN (freed reproduction from standing water)\n    │\n    ├── GYMNOSPERMS (naked seeds, ~1,000 species)\n    │   ├── Conifers (pine, spruce, fir, larch — dominant boreal forests)\n    │   ├── Cycads (Jurassic relicts)\n    │   ├── Ginkgo (single living species)\n    │   └── Gnetophytes (Ephedra, Welwitschia)\n    │\n    └── ANGIOSPERMS (flowering plants, ~300,000 species)\n        │   ← Innovation: FLOWERS (coevolution with pollinators)\n        │   ← Innovation: FRUITS (seed dispersal mutualism)\n        │   ← Innovation: DOUBLE FERTILIZATION (triploid endosperm)\n        │\n        ├── Monocots (~90,000 spp): grasses, lilies, orchids, palms\n        │   Features: parallel veins, fibrous roots, 3-merous flowers\n        │\n        └── Eudicots (~200,000 spp): most flowering plants\n            Features: net veins, taproot option, 4-5-merous flowers\n            Rosids: roses, oaks, legumes, brassicas, apples\n            Asterids: composites, mints, nightshades, carrots\n```"
    },
