        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Botany - Overview: The Plant Kingdom",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "DERMAL TISSUE SYSTEM       GROUND TISSUE SYSTEM       VASCULAR TISSUE SYSTEM\n─────────────────────      ────────────────────       ──────────────────────\nEpidermis:                 Parenchyma:                Xylem:\n  Single cell layer          Most abundant type         Water + mineral transport\n  Cuticle (wax coating)      Photosynthesis             Dead at maturity:\n  Stomata (guard cells)      Storage                    tracheids + vessels\n  Root hairs                 Wound healing              (one-way: root → leaf)\n  Trichomes (leaf hairs)\n                           Collenchyma:               Phloem:\nPeriderm (secondary):        Living support             Sugar transport\n  Cork cells (dead)          Pectin-thick walls         Alive: sieve tubes\n  Replaces epidermis         Celery \"strings\"           + companion cells\n  in woody plants            Corners reinforced         (source → sink, both ways)"
    },
